{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789228481,"nonce":"2Ou9BllCoNZVNeJ5bL5WkYzmecs=","message":"Direction corrected by the owner: ash must not depend on caribou. The\nbranch that made ash_std consume caribou (gc.rs and fiber.rs as\nforwarders) is withdrawn and kept only as a stash in the caribou-heap\nworktree. Its verification stands as evidence that the core heap and\nscheduler are behaviour-identical to ash's.\n\nThe relationship is a seam: ash keeps its collector and scheduler and\nexposes ash_std::rt, a versioned repr(C) table of function-pointer slots\nwith ash's implementations as defaults and hlp_rt_install to replace them\nbefore the first allocation (ash issue 0864a7a, in progress on that\nbranch). A caribou-ash adapter crate in this repo depends on ash, fills\nthe table with the core's heap and scheduler, and runs ash programs on\nthem. Ash's own suite keeps running against ash's own code.","files":null}]}